.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-recover 1  "recover " 
.SH NAME
murk\-recover \- Print the BIP39 recovery phrase for your age key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk recover\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the BIP39 recovery phrase for your age key
.PP
murk uses the key from `MURK_KEY`, `MURK_KEY_FILE` or the stored key for `.murk`. SSH keys and plugin identities have no recovery phrase.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
